computer_science.question:
An integer c is a common divisor of two integers x and y if and only if c is a divisor of x and c is a divisor of y. Which of the following sets of integers could possibly be the set of all common divisors of two integers?

A. {-6,-2, -1, 1, 2, 6}
B. {-6, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 6}
C. {-6, -3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3, 6}
D. {-6, -3, -2, -1, 0, 1, 2, 3, 6}

Which PyTorch 1.8 command(s) produce $10\times 5$ Gaussian matrix with each entry i.i.d. sampled from $\mathcal{N}(\mu=5,\sigma^2=16)$ and a $10\times 10$ uniform matrix with each entry i.i.d. sampled from $U[-1,1)$?

A. \texttt{5 + torch.randn(10,5) * 16} ; \texttt{torch.rand(10,10,low=-1,high=1)}
B. \texttt{5 + torch.randn(10,5) * 16} ; \texttt{(torch.rand(10,10) - 0.5) / 0.5}
C. \texttt{5 + torch.randn(10,5) * 4} ; \texttt{2 * torch.rand(10,10) - 1}
D. \texttt{torch.normal(torch.ones(10,5)*5,torch.ones(5,5)*16)} ; \texttt{2 * torch.rand(10,10) - 1}

math.question:
When three standard dice are tossed, the numbers $a,b,c$ are obtained. Find the probability that $abc = 180$.

A. \frac{1}{30}
B. \frac{1}{72}
C. \frac{1}{71}
D. \frac{1}{70}

A bag has 4 red and 6 blue marbles. A marble is selected and not replaced, then a second is selected. What is the probability that both are the same color?

A. \frac{1}{8}
B. \frac{8}{15}
C. \frac{1}{15}
D. \frac{7}{15}

Three points are chosen randomly and independently on a circle. What is the probability that all three pairwise distances between the points are less than the radius of the circle?

A. \frac{1}{20}
B. \frac{1}{32}
C. \frac{1}{12}
D. \frac{1}{16}
